# Branches of the "stopping" state that a real stop races past, reached deterministically with the runner's hold/blind hooks:
# the write thread processes a queued packet while stopping is set. Packet with sys_ts (pause_offset + dts in ns) below stop_ts is
# still written; at or above it is dropped. QUIRK: the encoder callback compares sys_dts_usec (microseconds) with stop_ts
# (nanoseconds) while the write thread compares nanoseconds.
create
world pause_offset 1000
start
pkt v 0 0 0 1 3000
pkt a 0 0 0 1 200
drain
state
hold on
blind 1
pkt v 0 3 3 0 800
stop_async 100000000
hold off
wait
state
# second run: stop_ts far above the packet's system time -> the in-flight packet is still written (total_bytes counts it)
start
pkt v 0 0 0 1 3000
pkt a 0 0 0 1 200
drain
hold on
blind 1
pkt v 0 3 3 0 800
stop_async 900000000
hold off
wait
state
